meehan@mozilla.com"}, "56": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr128 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes -  a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217740", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/translations-models.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8e095303761d3ce08438f1a36dcdf324b7b24f7a", "parents": ["b42bd2daa7feb5f12f89337b0ddd4c7380b64d60"], "tags": []}], "date": 1721929947, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "57": {"changesets": [{"author": "Neil Deakin \u003cneil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1904593, don't clear the autofill state when modified by script, r=dom-core,credential-management-reviewers,dimi,sefeng, a=dmeehan\n\nIt turns out that many sites are modifying the field state immediately after a value has been autofilled, typically to format the value such as add spaces between parts of a credit card number\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D215113", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/address/browser_autofill_whenhidden.js", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a8603822753b077f854e9f7cb9286634046953ba", "parents": ["8e095303761d3ce08438f1a36dcdf324b7b24f7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1905426 - Refine zero-scroll-offset scroll anchoring heuristic to match blink. r=hiro, a=dmeehan\n\nSee link in the comment. We were checking both offsets, but blink only\nchecks one.\n\nIn this case, the page has a table with `overflow-x: auto` and\n`overflow-y: hidden`. They implement a custom virtual scrolling on the\nvertical axis, and scroll-anchoring interacts poorly with it.\n\nAdapt zero-scroll-offset.html to test for this.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217201", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollAnchorContainer.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a7c5b9a3dc5f6e4e054c27277eacdeaae5b60767", "parents": ["a8603822753b077f854e9f7cb9286634046953ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1909395 - Adjust expectations of a new test. r=dholbert, a=test-only\n\nIn the \"regressing\" bug, I:\n\n * renamed zero-scroll-offset.html -\u003e zero-scroll-offset-001.html\n * created zero-scroll-offset-002.html, which is effectively the same\n   test but with an horizontal offset too.\n\nIt seems the test I based this off was flaky on Linux.\n\nFor now, update the expectations to deal with them. Needs more\ninvestigation to properly fix tho, but this flaky is not a _real_\nregression.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217512", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "79e5194eb0a4f268e1d7d4fac999e6f89896b50a", "parents": ["a7c5b9a3dc5f6e4e054c27277eacdeaae5b60767"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1909395 - Test is intermittently failing on windows too. a=test-only", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-anchoring/zero-scroll-offset-002.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "70521747dd4220601ec3949ff1aefeea6a205250", "parents": ["79e5194eb0a4f268e1d7d4fac999e6f89896b50a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1721998799, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "58": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jiaxun Yang \u003cjiaxun.yang@flygoat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1909793: Implement MacroAssembler::move8ZeroExtend for mips  a=dmeehan\n\nPort D197690 for MIPS.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jiaxun Yang \u003cjiaxun.yang@flygoat.com\u003e\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217672\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217779", "files": ["js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared-inl.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1fb051404133e3508d1ebd93151a5ef2f7d0fc16", "parents": ["70521747dd4220601ec3949ff1aefeea6a205250"], "tags": []}], "date": 1722017013, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "59": {"changesets": [{"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1909241 - shim updates;  a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217757", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/facebook-sdk.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/live-test-shim.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/mochitest-shim-1.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/mochitest-shim-2.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/rambler-authenticator.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/vidible.js", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/webcompat/src/main/assets/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/webcompat/src/main/assets/extensions/webcompat/shims/facebook-sdk.js", "mobile/and